1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
After a stroke on the right side of the brain, many people stop noticing the left half of the world.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,000
They eat half the plate. Read half the page. And usually, they don't know it. It's called left spatial neglect.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Therapists train it with paper sheets in the clinic. But in one Indian study, only 7.6% of stroke survivors got therapy at all.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Purna brings that exercise home, onto your own dining table, through Snap SPECS.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Small clay diyas appear. Light the whole ones with a pinch. Leave the chipped ones alone.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:50,000
No score. No timer. No failure sounds. Just lamps.

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Ramesh lights the right half, and stops. He's sure he's done.

8
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:12,000
The bell comes from the left. It points to the side, never to the answer. The searching stays his.

9
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
And as he starts finding the left on his own, the beam fades.

10
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
When the table is done, a thread replays his search. For the first time, he can see the half he skipped.

11
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Showing people where they looked improved neglect in a crossover study. Here it's on his own table.

12
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Four measures in plain words. Practice result, not a diagnosis. One pinch sends it home.

13
00:01:52,000 --> 00:02:04,000
His family types the code once. Every session arrives as one sentence and a trend line, the left side coming back.

14
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:12,000
The therapist gets a seven-day link with every number a cancellation test gives, and writes a note back.

15
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
And the site explains what the numbers mean.

16
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Every rule is plain TypeScript, tested before Lens Studio opened. CLAD built the scene from our plan-lens brief, and LEAF checks each done criterion.

17
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Three simulated searchers on two hundred tables prove the report tells left neglect from object neglect. 181 automated tests run on every change.

18
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Purna is a practice tool, not a medical device, and it hasn't met a patient yet. That's next.

19
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Purna. Whole.
